## Development

```sh
{% if 'python' in stacks %}uv sync{% if python_dir != '.' %} --directory {{ python_dir }}{% endif %}
{% endif %}{% if 'ts' in stacks %}pnpm{% if ts_dir != '.' %} -C {{ ts_dir }}{% endif %} install
{% endif %}{% if 'rust' in stacks %}cargo install --locked cargo-nextest cargo-deny   # once per machine
{% endif %}{% if 'go' in stacks %}curl -sSfL https://golangci-lint.run/install.sh | sh -s -- -b "$(go env GOPATH)/bin" {{ golangci_lint_version }}   # once per machine
{% endif %}{% if 'ts' in stacks and 'python' not in stacks %}pnpm{% if ts_dir != '.' %} -C {{ ts_dir }}{% endif %} exec prek install     # git hooks
{% else %}uv tool install prek   # once per machine
prek install     # git hooks
{% endif %}```

`just` lists the tasks. They mirror what [.github/workflows/](.github/workflows/) runs.

```sh
just check       # lint, types and tests for every stack here{% if 'python' in stacks and kind == 'data-pipeline' %}
just pipeline    # fetch, build and validate every source in sources.toml{% endif %}{% if 'docker' in stacks %}
just up          # run each service in its container, rebuilt on source changes{% endif %}
```
{% if 'python' in stacks and kind == 'data-pipeline' %}{% set d = '' if python_dir == '.' else python_dir ~ '/' %}
## Pipeline

[`{{ d }}sources.toml`]({{ d }}sources.toml) declares every input: its URL, its reuse
terms, and whether the pipeline reads it yet (`status`). `just fetch` downloads each
implemented source to `{{ d }}data/raw/` with a fetch record, `just build` writes
`{{ d }}data/processed/`, and `just validate` checks the published output against those
records. Neither directory is committed. [ATTRIBUTION.md](ATTRIBUTION.md) lists what
this repository reuses, and on what terms.
